{
  "_doc": "Each rule gives one skill to a task when ALL listed 'when' groups match (any value within a group). 'unless' uses the same groups and cancels the rule. Higher priority wins; ties keep file order. Groups: roles, kinds, globs (match paths in scope or their file names), keywords (whole-word match in task text), all_keywords, flags (router booleans). Put personal overrides in ~/.claude/feature-ladder/skill-rules.json and per-project ones in <repo>/.feature-ladder/skill-rules.json; reuse an id to replace a rule, or list ids under 'disable'. Rules sharing a 'group' are alternatives (e.g. a Claude Code skill and its Claude app equivalent): only the highest-priority installed one is used. 'max_chars_by_role' caps the characters of skill text per router role (0 = no skill text); roles not listed use 'max_chars'. Rules are kept in step with the skills that are actually installed: `select_skills.py --scan` lists rules whose skill is gone and installed skills no rule reaches.",
  "max_skills": 3,
  "max_chars": 20000,
  "max_chars_by_role": {"mechanic": 0, "codex-reviewer": 0, "memory-scribe": 0, "evidence-collector": 10000, "implementer": 8000, "senior-implementer": 30000, "domain-expert": 30000, "domain-expert-high": 30000, "deep-verifier": 15000, "architect-escalation": 30000},
